rlm-git-status [-c|--changed] [-b|--base <ref>] [-P|--no-pr] [-J|--no-jira] [<directory>]

Status table across every git repo in a directory, one row per repo.
Written for the multi-repo collection dirs created by rlm-pr-worktree's
multi-repo mode — one directory holding a worktree of every repo on a
shared branch — where the questions are "what in this change set is
still unfinished?" and "which repos have a PR, and which are still
only local?"

rlm-git-repos is an alias for this function. The two were separate
before — a verbose local-work view and an inventory view — and were
merged, since they shared their scanning, divergence and rendering
logic and differed only in which columns they added.

Scans the immediate children of <directory> (default: the current
directory), treating each child that is its own git worktree root as a
member. When the target is itself a repo and has no repo children, it
reports on just that repo, so the function also works as a plain
status summary from inside a single worktree.

COLUMNS
  REPO      Directory name of the member repo.
  BRANCH    Current branch, or "(detached <sha>)". Truncated with an
            ellipsis past 38 characters so long collection branches do
            not wrap the table. Hidden when every repo shares one
            branch, which is then shown in the header instead.
  AHEAD/BEHIND
            Commit divergence from the base branch, shown as +N
            (ahead), -N (behind), both, "=" when in sync, or "?" when
            the base ref does not exist in that repo.
  LOCAL     Uncommitted work, broken down as conflict / staged /
            unstaged / untracked counts, or "clean".
  PR        Pull request number for the branch, as an OSC 8 hyperlink
            to the PR. Colored by state: green open, cyan merged, red
            closed. "-" when the branch has no PR.
  JIRA      Issue key parsed from the branch name (falling back to a
            key embedded in the collection dirname), as an OSC 8
            hyperlink, followed by the cached "(Status) Summary" when
            one is available. "-" when no key can be found. Hidden
            when every repo shares one key, which is then shown in the
            header instead.

These dimensions are independent — a repo can be any combination of
them, and collapsing to one "differs" boolean would hide the
interesting cases: work committed but no PR, or a PR open while the
tree is still dirty.

By default every repo gets a row. Pass --changed to narrow the table
to repos that have uncommitted work or have diverged from the base;
the rest then collapse onto one dim "unchanged:" line, which is the
useful view once a collection grows past a handful of repos. Repo
names on that line are abbreviated by stripping a shared boilerplate
prefix (data-platform-) when one is long enough to be worth removing.

The base ref defaults to origin/<default branch>, read from
origin/HEAD and falling back to origin/main. Nothing is ever fetched,
so divergence is measured against the remote-tracking refs as they
stand locally — run `git fetch` first if they may be stale.

Repos are probed in parallel, which matters because the `gh pr list`
call dominates: seven repos serially take several seconds, in parallel
well under one. Pass --no-pr to skip the network entirely.

JIRA summaries are served from ~/.cache/wts-jira/<KEY>.summary, the
same cache wt-preview and wt-collection-preview populate, refreshed on
a 3-day TTL when `acli` is available. Members of a collection share a
key, so it is looked up once rather than once per repo.

Colors and hyperlinks are emitted only when stdout is a terminal, so
the table stays pasteable when piped or redirected. Inside tmux, OSC 8
hyperlinks need `set -ga terminal-features "*:hyperlinks"` in
~/.tmux.conf (already set in this dotfiles repo).

OPTIONS
  -c, --changed      List only repos with uncommitted work or
                     divergence from the base, collapsing the rest
                     onto an "unchanged:" line.
  -a, --all          Accepted as a no-op: listing every repo is the
                     default. Kept so the pre-merge spelling still
                     works.
  -b, --base <ref>   Compare against <ref> instead of
                     origin/<default branch>.
  -P, --no-pr        Skip PR lookups. Also implied when `gh` or `jq`
                     is not on PATH.
  -J, --no-jira      Skip the JIRA column.
  -h, --help         Print a usage line.

EXAMPLES
  git-status ~/git/work/StorytelDataPlatform_20260730_DATA-2770-foo
  git-status                      # current directory
  git-status --changed            # hide clean, in-sync repos
  git-status --no-pr              # offline, no gh calls
  git-status --base origin/develop

REQUIRES
  git, and optionally gh + jq (PR column) and acli (JIRA summaries)
